# Corpus manifest: how each fixture is classified for the family conformance suite
# (conformance_test.go). One line per file: <kind> <format> <file>.
#   clean     compacts on exit 0 as <format>; the output must be strictly shorter.
#   preserve  must come back byte-identical (failures, warnings, truncation,
#             CRLF, terminal escapes other than colour, binary, or any shape
#             a summary would drop facts from).
# <format> is the compressor.Format the fixture belongs to ("unknown" when no
# family owns it). A new family adds its fixtures here; the test needs no edit.
# Every file in this directory must be listed, and every line must name a file.
